<<~ ahu slot=`#/per-red`>>

!! Per red
# e2e floor-user-wiki-refuses W0/W1/W2, session-sign-reach S1/S2, node-b face-cell-lights-proved C0 — PRODUCT WAS WRONG.
Root: `SlotDocResolver.bindings` (keyhive slot-doc-resolver.ts) still minted a working slot for every wiki; at a faceless
floor `workingDoc` threw `no-face` through the island binding reply, so the floor's `lares` mount died before wiki-ready.
Cure: bindings answers `workingUrl: null` without a face (slotDoc still refuses `no-face`; nothing founds). Threaded:
daemon-behavior omits the url, daemon-vm-core settles null (host daemon working layer refuses by name if null),
vessel-steps/core-caps types, mesh `mountWikiSlot` lays no working layer → no default writable, writes refuse
NoWorkingLayerRefusal by name. No floor anchor / floor working doc resurrected.
2a. keyhive floor-refuses-content-verbs (2 tests) — TEST STALE. Since the workbench lane the floor verifierFactory always
attaches the daemon wiki's device-slot working layer; the fake ctx lacked `recipe`. Test now passes a floor ctx where
that layer already stands; verifier assertions unchanged.
2b. browser vessel-worker-seams census — false positives in browser-floor-pin.ts (`document (` in refusal prose,
`b.alert(`). Port renamed `raiseAlert` (open-browser-vessel + floor-pin test updated), prose reworded. No page global reached.
3b. node-b faced-boot-requires-proof (browser) — the pre-walk face-label block pushed `keepBrowserFaceAnchor(idbName, pinned)`
past the weld's 3000-char window. Label write moved after the pin (proof → pin → label). Now 2677 chars.
# web-tw5 wiki-mount-private-alias — TEST STALE: workbench commit 80f3f0719 designates `personal` for mirroring on purpose;
test now asserts it is included.
# seed-census K15 — floor.ts / floor-cut.ts read loadVesselVerifyingKey() for the publication board, same as nexus-release
(already `place`). Receipted as `place`, count 1 each. (floor-unlock-door F1w in that log is a todo, not a fail.)

<<~/ahu>>

